ml_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/5335#issuecomment-5142113952","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/5335","id":5142113952,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs8AAAABMn5uoA","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-31T10:56:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T10:56:16Z","body":"# PR review\n\nNo merge-blocking issues found. The new submenu focus branching in `MenuPopup` holds up across the paths I traced: hover opens (`triggerHover` reason) and ArrowKey opens (`listNavigation`) keep `initialFocus` disabled as before, Enter/Space are excluded via `openMethod === 'keyboard'`, virtual (screen reader) presses are excluded via the new `virtualPress` flag, and only physical press-opens now focus the popup — which is the intended fix. The `virtualPress` lifecycle is sound: `onPointerDown` always rewrites the flag before the `mousedown`-driven open, the close reset in `MenuSubmenuTrigger` covers normal closes, and the store is recreated on remount, so I couldn't construct a stale-flag scenario that affects behavior. `Store.set` bails on unchanged values, so the per-pointerdown write costs nothing. One test-coverage nit below.\n\n## Tests (1)\n\n### 1. 🟡 The VoiceOver press-open path is untested; the existing \"pointer\" VO test actually opens via hover\n\n**Location:** `packages/react/src/menu/submenu-trigger/MenuSubmenuTrigger.voiceOver.test.tsx:95`\n\n```tsx\nit('keeps the expanded state when the submenu is opened with a pointer', async () => {\n  ...\n  await user.click(submenuTrigger);\n```\n\nIn this test the submenu trigger uses the default `openOnHover={true}`, and `useClick` is configured with `ignoreMouse: openOnHover`, so the mouse press itself never opens the submenu — the open comes from the hover interaction (`triggerHover` reason) triggered by the pointer movement of `user.click`. That was fine before, but this PR makes press-opens and hover-opens behaviorally distinct (press-opens now focus the popup and go through the `virtualPress`/`openMethod` exclusions), and the physical press + VoiceOver combination — where `aria-expanded` should be *kept* while focus moves to the popup — has no test.\n\n**Failure scenario:** A future change to the `focusMovesToSubmenuItem` condition (e.g. accidentally treating all `triggerPress` opens as focus-moving) would omit `aria-expanded` for physical pointer presses without any test failing, since the only \"pointer\" VO test never exercises the press-open code path.\n\n**Fix:** Add a VO test with `openOnHover={false}` that clicks the trigger and asserts `aria-expanded` remains `\"true\"` (and optionally that the popup receives focus). Consider renaming the existing test to \"opened by hover\" to match what it exercises.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**Approve after nits** - the focus logic is correct across all open paths; only a test-coverage gap on the new press-open/VoiceOver boundary remains.\n\n---\n\n🤖 Review 